   292	## 5. THEOREM DEV-FREE: the deviation variables, and why the ladder was the
   293	wrong bookkeeping
   294	
   295	### 5.1 The universal ray is the shadow of the `kappa = 0` family
   296	
   297	The corrected leading-order kernel `(x,y,w) = (n/4, 3/4, 1)` is `c`-independent:
   298	`r_n = s_sigma^2/(4b eta_e^2)`, `q_m = 3a s_sigma^2/(4b^2 eta_e)`. Lead (L3) asks
   299	whether `q` and `r` are `s^2/eta`-type expressions. They are, and the reason is
   300	sharp: substituting the *exact* ansatz `s = eta u`, `q = 3a eta u^2/(4b^2)`,
   301	`r = u^2/(4b)` (which makes `T1` automatic) into the corrected system gives
   302	
   303	```text
   304	   EQ1  =  2 Z kappa ,          EQ4  =  kappa E1 ,
   305	   EQ2, EQ3, O1s  =  explicit expressions in (eta, G) alone (EQ2, EQ3) resp.
   306	                     (eta, s, G) with a  4Z b^3 kappa eta^4  term (O1s).
   307	```
   308	
   309	**Every `(eta, s, G)`-dependence of `EQ1` cancels identically on the ray.** The
   310	ray is exactly the leading order of the `kappa = 0` solution family, and `kappa`
   311	is the whole obstruction. That is the structural statement the order-by-order
   312	ladder could not see.
   313	
   314	### 5.2 The deviations
   315	
   316	Put
   317	
   318	```text
   319	   X := 4b eta^2 r - s^2 ,        Y := 4b^2 eta q - 3a s^2 ,
   320	```
   321	
   322	equivalently `r = (s^2+X)/(4b eta^2)`, `q = (3a s^2+Y)/(4b^2 eta)`. In the
   323	simultaneous-top regime `deg(4b eta^2 r) = deg(4b^2 eta q) = deg s^2 = 2 sigma`,
   324	and the ray is exactly the vanishing of the degree-`2sigma` coefficients of `X`
   325	and `Y`.
   326	
   327	> **RAY-1 restated.** RAY's entire order-`(top-1)` residual — the pins
   328	> `eta_{e-1}/eta_e = beta - delta/2`, `s_{sigma-1}/s_sigma = beta`,
   329	> `q_{m-1}/q_m = beta + delta/2`, `r_{n-1}/r_n = delta` — is precisely
   330	> ```text
   331	>       deg X <= 2 sigma - 2   and   deg Y <= 2 sigma - 2 .
   332	> ```
   333	> *Proof.* `[Z^{2sigma-1}]X = s_sigma^2(2 alpha + delta - 2 beta)` and
   334	> `[Z^{2sigma-1}]Y = 3a s_sigma^2(alpha + gamma - 2 beta)`, using
   335	> `4b eta_e^2 r_n = s_sigma^2` and `4b^2 eta_e q_m = 3a s_sigma^2`. Both vanish
   336	> exactly on RAY's two-parameter solution. QED
   337	
   338	So the "four conditions on five new coefficients per order" bookkeeping is an
   339	artefact of the coordinates: in `(eta, s, G, X, Y)` the free objects at each
   340	order are only `X` and `Y`, and the number of *conditions* is five.
   341	
