   389	## 6. THEOREM A2-DEV-BOUND: a uniform, U-free bound
   390	
   391	Fix `xi := deg X`, `ups := deg Y`, `k := max(xi, ups)`, and let
   392	`c := G_g/(b eta_e^2)` in Chamber II. All degrees and leaders below were
   393	computed with **generic** truncated tails (symbolic sub-leading coefficients),
   394	not by monomial substitution, so no vanished leader is hidden.
   395	
   396	### 6.1 The two rows and the two inhomogeneities
   397	
   398	```text
   399	  deg Lambda_1 = max(2e,g) + e + k - 1 ,
   400	     leader (Chamber II) = (k-2e) b eta_e^3 [ 3a(3c+6e+2) X_k - 4(c+2e+1) Y_k ] ;
   401	  deg Psi_1    = 2e + 1  exactly  (the term 8Z b^2 kappa eta^2, kappa != 0).
   402	
   403	  deg Lambda_3 = e + k + 1 ,
   404	     leader = (k-2e) eta_e [ 3a X_k - 2 Y_k ]      (no c, no chamber) ;
   405	  deg Psi_3    = 5e             (Chambers II and III)
   406	             or  e + 2g          (Chamber I),
   407	     leader   = 3a b^2 eta_e^5 P(c)                (Chamber II),
   408	                12a b^2 eta_e^5 e^2 (2e-1)          (Chamber III),
   409	                -3a eta_e G_g^2 (1+2e+2g)           (Chamber I),
   410	     P(c) := 4e^2(2e-1) + 4ce(2e-1) - c^2(6e+1)     [HF Sec 4.4, reproduced].
   411	```
   412	
   413	Both `Lambda` leaders were checked ratio-`1` against the displayed closed forms
   414	at twelve `(e,k)` pairs, `1<=e<=3`; the three `Psi_3` leaders ratio-`1` at
   415	fourteen `(e,g)` pairs. `deg V = 3e-2` (generic) was checked at `e=1..4`, which
   416	is what puts `2VY` strictly below `4E1 N(Y)`.
   417	
   418	### 6.2 The descent
   419	
   420	The `Lambda_1` and `Lambda_3` rows are *homogeneous* (their inhomogeneity is
   421	strictly lower) exactly when
   422	
   423	```text
   424	   EQ1 :  max(2e,g) + e + k - 1 > 2e+1        <=>   k >= 3 - e   (all chambers)
   425	   EQ3 :  e + k + 1 > 5e                      <=>   k >= 4e      (Ch. II, III)
   426	          e + k + 1 > e + 2g                  <=>   k >= 2g      (Ch. I)
   427	```
   428	
   429	and their `2x2` determinant is
   430	
   431	```text
   432	   Chamber II (g = 2e) :  -6a (k-2e)^2 (c + 2e)
   433	   Chamber III (g < 2e) :  -6a e (k-2e)^2
   434	   Chamber I  (g > 2e) :  -6a (k-2e)^2 G_g
   435	```
   436	
   437	(the Chamber III/I entries use `lead(E1) = b(1+2e)eta_e^2` resp. `G_g` and
   438	`lead(3E1-b eta^2) = b(6e+2) eta_e^2` resp. `3G_g`). Hence:
   439	
   440	> **THEOREM A2-DEV-BOUND.** On the live section (`G != 0`, `s != 0`, `e >= 1`,
   441	> `a b kappa != 0`), in the simultaneous-top regime,
   442	>
   443	> ```text
   444	>   Chamber III (g < 2e) :   deg X <= 4e-1 ,  deg Y <= 4e-1 .   Unconditional.
   445	>   Chamber II  (g = 2e) :   deg X <= 4e-1 ,  deg Y <= 4e-1 ,   provided c != -2e.
   446	>   Chamber I   (g > 2e) :   deg X <= 2g-1 ,  deg Y <= 2g-1 .   Unconditional.
   447	> ```
   448	>
   449	> *Proof.* For `k >= 4e` (resp. `2g`) both rows are homogeneous and, since
   450	> `k >= 4e > 2e` (resp. `k >= 2g > 2e`), the factor `(k-2e)` is nonzero; the
   451	> determinant is then nonzero under the stated proviso, so `X_k = Y_k = 0`.
   452	> Descend. `k >= 3-e` holds throughout since `k >= 4e >= 4`. QED
   453	
   454	This is the first statement in the horn lane that bounds anything **uniformly in
   455	`U`**. It is the exact answer to the charge's "prove a bound"; what it bounds is
   456	not `U` itself but the deviation from the ray, and Sec 7 converts that.
