   466	## 7. THEOREM A2-U-BOUND: what actually bounds `U`, and what does not
   467	
   468	### 7.1 `EQ4`'s row is homogeneous at every level
   469	
   470	From `(D2)` and the `Lambda_4` display,
   468	### 7.1 `EQ4`'s row is homogeneous at every level
   469	
   470	From `(D2)` and the `Lambda_4` display,
   471	
   472	```text
   473	   deg Psi_4 = deg(kappa E1) = 2e ,
   474	   deg Q_4   = xi + ups - e - 1 ,
   475	   deg Lambda_4 = k + 2 sigma - e - 1     (verified generically, 18 cells).
   476	```
   477	
   478	In the regime `U >= 3e`, i.e. `2 sigma = U + e >= 4e`, and with `k <= 4e-1`:
   479	
   480	```text
   481	   Lambda_4 > Q_4  <=>  k + 2 sigma > xi + ups ;   xi+ups <= 2k and 2 sigma >= 4e > k. OK
   482	   Lambda_4 > Psi_4 <=> k + 2 sigma > 3e + 1 ;     2 sigma >= 4e > 3e+1 for e >= 2,
   483	                                                    and for e = 1 whenever U >= 5.
   484	```
   485	
   486	> **THEOREM A2-EQ4-HOM.** In the simultaneous-top regime the `EQ4` deviation row
   487	> is homogeneous at every level `k >= 0`. Its exact form (normalised by
   488	> `s_sigma^2/(8 eta_e b^2)`) is
   489	> ```text
   490	>    [ 3a(k-2e) ,  -2( (sigma-e) c + k + 2e(sigma-e-1) ) ] .
   491	> ```
   492	
   493	This row was *derived* from the closed form of `Lambda_4` and then checked at 36
   494	`(e,sigma,k)` triples, `1<=e<=3`: exact agreement including the `sigma`-columns.
   495	
   496	### 7.2 The dichotomy
   497	
   498	Let `k = max(xi, ups)` and assume `c != -2e` and `c != -(2e+1)`. The `EQ1` row
   499	is homogeneous throughout because `k >= 3-e` fails only for `k <= 2-e`, i.e.
   500	`k <= 1` at `e = 1` and never for `e >= 3`; those finitely many small-`k`
   501	configurations are inside branch (B)'s bound `k <= 2e` and are not used below.
   502	
   503	* **`ups > xi` is impossible.** Only `Y_ups` survives; `EQ1`'s `Y`-entry forces
   504	  `(ups-2e)(c+2e+1) = 0`, so `ups = 2e`; then `EQ4`'s `Y`-entry is
   505	  `-2(sigma-e)(c+2e)`, nonzero because `sigma > e` and `c != -2e`. Contradiction.
   506	* **`xi > ups` forces `xi = 2e`.** Only `X_xi` survives, and each of the `EQ1`,
   507	  `EQ3`, `EQ4` `X`-entries carries the factor `(xi - 2e)`.
   508	* **`xi = ups = k`.** The `EQ1`/`EQ4` determinant is
   509	
   510	  ```text
   511	     det(EQ1,EQ4) = -6a (k-2e) * R ,
   512	     R := (c+2e)[(3c+6e+2) sigma + k] - e(3c+6e+2)(c+2e+2) + 4e(c+2e+1)
   513	  ```
   514	
   515	  (verified: `det + 6a(k-2e)R = 0` identically). So `k = 2e` or `R = 0`.
   516	
   517	> **THEOREM A2-U-BOUND.** Live section, Chamber II, `U >= 3e`,
   518	> `c not in {-2e, -(2e+1)}`. Then exactly one of
   519	>
   520	> ```text
   521	>  (A)  xi = ups = k <= 4e-1  and  R(e,c,sigma,k) = 0 ;
   522	>  (B)  xi = 2e ,  ups < 2e   (the N-degenerate branch).
   523	> ```
   524	>
   525	> In branch (A), if `3c+6e+2 != 0` then `R = 0` reads
