   195	## 4. RAY-1 N2 and RAY-2
   196	
   197	On the Wall-B ray, I extracted the order-one-deeper rows by Laurent expansion at
   198	infinity.  For `U>=3e+2`, at `e=1,2,3,4`, the rows match:
   199	
   200	```text
   201	N3:  beta - gamma + delta/2 = 0
   202	N1:  alpha - beta + delta/2 = 0
   203	N4:  n alpha - 2 beta - (n-2) gamma + (n-1) delta = 0
   204	```
   205	
   206	Old `N2` is exactly RAY's measured row:
   207	
   208	```text
   209	N2old = (2n-2e-3)alpha - 2(3n+2e-4)beta
   210	        + (4n+2e-5)gamma - (n-1)delta - epshat.
   211	```
   212	
   213	Correcting `EQ2` changes it to
   214	
   215	```text
   216	N2corr = (2n+2e-3)alpha - 2(3n+2e-4)beta
   217	         + (4n+2e-5)gamma - (n-1)delta.
   218	```
   219	
   220	There is no `epshat` term.  Substituting `N1` and `N3` into `N2corr` gives `0`
   221	identically.  Hence `epshat` is not constrained at this order and
   222	
   223	```text
   224	RAY-2: REFUTED.  The statement deg E1 <= 2e-2 is not derived.
   225	Surviving wall statement: deg E1 <= 2e-1 only.
   226	Residual dimension: 3 parameters (beta, delta, epshat), not 2.
   227	```
   228	
   229	With the independent T2 sign correction, the boundary slice `U=3e` has a changed
   230	inhomogeneity.  In normalized variables `a=b=eta_e=s_sigma=1`, the corrected
   231	`N3` equation is
   232	
   233	```text
   234	beta - gamma + delta/2 = -1/2.
   235	```
   236	
   237	Equivalently the old `rho` formula is not valid; the corrected dimensional form
   238	is `rho = - b^2 eta_e^4/(2 s_sigma^2)`.  It is still nonzero, so RAY-DEP still
   239	kills `U=3e` for `e>=2` because
   240	
   241	```text
   242	n*N1 + (n-2)*N3 - N4 = -(n-2)*rho.
   243	```
   244	
   245	Thus `RAY-DEP` survives, and `RAY-EDGE(e>=2)` survives after replacing `rho`.
   246	The `(1,3)` edge cell remains a separate CAS cell; existing decisions used the
   247	old row package and must not be consumed for the fully corrected system.
