+`qqideal` was given an explicit `Ideal` already containing the Rabinowitsch
+row; its `.saturate()` method was never called. `msolveio` emitted every parser-
+safe payload. SymPy rebuilt the same ordered rational ideals independently.
+
+Execution deviation: an exploratory SymPy run on the *unlicensed capped probe*
+`e=2,c=-4` failed to terminate at the desk limit because its watchdog was not
+armed correctly; it was interrupted after 1463 seconds and returned no basis.
+No statement in this report consumes that run. This is another reason the
+global `c=-2e` row remains `OPEN`; any retry is a coordinator job with a hard
+timeout and, first, a licensed cap.
+
+The only nonempty object published here is the deliberately planted control,
+typed exactly
+
+```text
+artifact=SUBSYSTEM_POINT
+attainment=NECESSARY
+```
+
+No decided DEV locus survives. The open rows in Section 6 are problem scopes,
+not points. Nothing in this report is called a curve, a map, or a `(B3)`
+object. If a future `c=-2e` or Chamber-I subsystem point appears, it must pass,
+pointwise and before any promotion,
+
+```text
+eta^2 | s^2+X,
+eta   | 3a s^2+Y,
+s     | qr'-kappa/2,
