   238	form, versus `3Z^5` from the retired derivative form
   239	(`a2-e2-p0-gate-gpt55-20260902.md:108-125`).
   240	
   241	Multiplying `O1` by `s` and eliminating `p's` using `E0` gives
   242	
   243	```text
   244	O1s = 8s C2 r' - 8E2(qr'-kappa/2)
   245	    + 4s(C1 E1'-C1' E1)
   246	    + 6D1 s s' - 2D1' s^2
   247	    + 4Zs(qs'-q's) = 0,
   248	
   249	O1s = s O1 - 4E2 E0                                      (identity).
   250	```
   251	
   252	Thus no division by `s` occurs in the generator; equivalence with `O1` is
   253	asserted only later on the live `s!=0` section. This is the p-prime-free row
   254	requested in `a2-ubound-opus5-20260902.md:257-283`.
   255	
   256	For the determinant checksum put
   257	
   258	```text
   259	W = q s'-q's,
   260	T = -(C1 E1'-C1' E1)/2 - 3D1 s'/4 + D1' s/4 - ZW/2,
   261	
   262	DET_EO = (sC1-qE1)T + (W/2)(sC2-qE2)
   263	       + (kappa/2)(E1C2-C1E2).
   264	```
   265	
   266	This is exactly the augmented determinant of the three affine rows in
   267	`(r',p')`, so `E0=O0=O1=0` implies `DET_EO=0`. The generator exact-diffs its
   268	determinantal syzygy. It is a checksum, not an additional ideal generator, as
   269	required by `ideation-20260902T0741Z-sol56.md:163-217`.
