   411	## 5. The coefficient ideals and exact projection
   412	
   413	On the charged live, simultaneous-top branch (A), for `e>=1` specialize
   414	`a=b=eta_e=1`, `c5=0`, and in Chamber II write
   415	
   416	```text
   417	eta = Z^e + sum(eta_j Z^j, 0<=j<e),
   418	G   = c Z^(2e) + sum(G_j Z^j, 0<=j<2e),
   419	X   = sum(X_j Z^j, 0<=j<4e),
   420	Y   = sum(Y_j Z^j, 0<=j<4e).
   421	```
   422	
   423	The cap `deg X,deg Y<=4e-1` is licensed in this scope in Chamber II only when
   424	`c!=-2e`, and in Chamber III unconditionally
   425	(`a2-e2-p0-gate-gpt55-20260902.md:280-301`). The coefficient ideal below is a
   426	necessary s-free subsystem in that scope, not a presentation of every point in
   427	the named chamber.
   428	The declared rational ring is exactly
   429	
   430	```text
   431	Q[eta_0..eta_(e-1), G_0..G_(2e-1), X_0..X_(4e-1),
   432	  Y_0..Y_(4e-1), kappa, tt, c],
   433	```
   434	
   435	with all variables except `c` in the first elimination block and `c` last.
   436	The adapter-safe map removes underscores only:
   437	
   438	```text
   439	eta_j -> etaj, G_j -> Gj, X_j -> Xj, Y_j -> Yj;
   440	kappa -> kappa, tt -> tt, c -> c.
   441	```
   442	
   443	Every image and the complete ordered generator list are emitted before a
   444	solver call. The ideal `I_e` is generated by every `Z` coefficient of
   445	`F1,F2,F3` and the explicit Rabinowitsch row
   446	
   447	```text
   448	kappa*c*(c+2e)*tt - 1 = 0.
   449	```
   450	
   451	No `sat()` or saturation wrapper occurs. The generator expands this row to
   452	parser-safe monomials before `msolveio` emission.
